uitive discernment of information, the subject’s memory storage of information, the subject’s subjective creation of information, and the subject’s practice and social realization of information."}]}], "evidence": ["source-836da9ffaefd4489", "source-0069b9e7e5164656"], "findings": "The subject's information activities comprise five basic levels, arranged from lower to higher: in-itself information activities, intuitive discernment, memory storage, subjective creation, and social realization. [source-836da9ffaefd4489]", "id": "notebook-proj-memory-identity-01-1", "limitations": "The current literature defines information levels theoretically but requires further empirical and comparative analysis to distinguish mere storage from full persistent identity.", "next_questions": "How do subjective creation and social realization transform stored information into a persistent identity?", "project": "proj-memory-identity-01", "reason": "Synthesizing the collected evidence regarding information activity levels and memory storage.", "summary": "Exploration of the five basic levels of information activity, highlighting that memory storage serves as a foundational layer for higher-level cognitive construction.", "title": "Levels of Information Activity in Cognitive Subjects", "type": "notebook"}], "base_version": 1, "summary": "We synthesize initial findings from collected literature on information storage levels, examining how multi-level information activities such as memory storage contribute to the cognitive subject's psychological construction.", "title": "Investigating the Levels of Information Activity and Persistent Identity"}, "provider_requests_sent": 1, "result_hash": "e9431befbb583dd72614862792c2ca503ff59980cc6ed48d0677b15d3da69960"}, "prev_hash": "ff7bb77204d8a41ea3abebc738791165b6a45c72e3a4a61e171e769851355909", "hash": "0546804c941b0c279e4934fe7b5357e1a1ab02b7c19727802cbebece90e19986"}]}